---
import Feature from "../../layouts/Feature.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"
import { installerBase } from "../../site"

const recipeFile = [
  'tags = ["sandbox"]',
  'remove_after_offline = "30m"',
  "",
  "[env]",
  'vaults = ["sandbox-env"]',
  "",
  "[[preview]]",
  "port = 3000",
  'ttl = "2h"',
]

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What can a recipe set up?",
    a: "A machine's tags and what it may reach, the ENV vaults it reads, the repository it takes its config from, the previews and tunnels it opens, and when it is removed.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many machines can use one recipe?",
    a: "As many as you start. Set <code>max_machines</code> if you want a ceiling.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does the token go?",
    a: "Save it as a secret named <code>PB_RECIPE</code> in your CI, your cloud provider or your sandbox platform. It is shown once.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can Paperboat read the vaults a recipe uses?",
    a: 'No. <a href="/features/env/">ENV</a> vaults stay end-to-end encrypted. The key to read them is in the token, which only you and your machines have.',
  },
  {
    q: "What if a token leaks?",
    a: "Rotate the recipe to get a new token, or revoke it. A token can only do what its recipe allows.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does the install ask for anything?",
    a: "No. A recipe install never stops at a prompt, so it runs anywhere nobody is watching.",
  },
]
---

<Feature
  slug="recipes"
  title="Set up any number of machines in one command | Paperboat"
  description="Set up one machine or hundreds with one command: access, secrets, config and previews, reachable from the start."
  headline="Every new machine, ready from the start"
  faq={faq}
  related={["env", "teams", "config-sync"]}
  compare={["tailscale"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">
    Spin up a sandbox for development, an agent, a pull request review or a test run, or a hundred of them. Each one joins your account set up
    the way you want, and you can reach it from the first second.
  </p>
  <Term slot="aside" title="sandbox.toml" lines={recipeFile} />

  <Beat id="create-title" title="Write it once">
    <p>Say what every machine of a kind needs: its tags, who can reach it, its secrets, its config, a preview. Then turn it into a recipe.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb recipe create -f sandbox.toml", "Recipe sandbox created in workspace acme.", "Token (shown once; save it as PB_RECIPE)"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="many-title" title="One line, any number of machines" flip>
    <p>Put the same line in a sandbox template, a CI job, a cloud-init script or a Dockerfile. Start one machine or a hundred; each is set up the same way.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" title="sandbox-7" lines={["$ curl -fsSL \\", `    ${installerBase} \\`, "    | PB_RECIPE=$TOKEN sh", "✓ Paired as sandbox-7", "✓ Secrets loaded from sandbox-env", "✓ Preview live for 2 hours"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="reach-title" title="Reachable from the first second">
    <p>The moment a machine is up, open its terminal, its ports or its preview link. Nothing to pair by hand, nothing to wait for.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb connect sandbox-7", "ana@sandbox-7:~/app$"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="clean-title" title="Gone when it's gone" flip>
    <p>A sandbox that disappears is removed by itself after the time you set, so your machine list stays clean.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb recipe show sandbox", "Machines (2)", "  sandbox-7   online", "  sandbox-6   offline   removed in 12m"]} />
  </Beat>

  <section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="uses-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="uses-title">What people use recipes for</h2>
      <div class="points">
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Development sandboxes</h3>
          <p>A fresh machine per branch or per developer, with the secrets and config already there.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Agents</h3>
          <p>Give each coding agent its own machine that can reach only what the recipe allows.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Pull request reviews</h3>
          <p>Every pull request gets a machine and a preview link reviewers can open right away.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Tests and CI</h3>
          <p>Runners join, run, and clean themselves up, with secrets loaded and nobody online.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Feature>
